{"format":"kards-original-reference","version":1,"id":"dbf34c602047f311","name":"card_event_dilemma","package":"/Game/Blueprints/Cards/Britain/NavalWarfare/events/card_event_dilemma","parent":"UBaseCardObject","card":{"title":"DILEMMA","text":"Swap the attack and operation cost of target unit.","flavorText":"The cracking of the German Enigma code, codenamed Program Ultra by the Allies, was one of the most closely guarded secrets of WWII and a turning point in the Allied campaign. The first breakthroughs came from Polish mathematicians, who succeeded in reconstructing early Enigma machines and passed their knowledge to British and French intelligence just before the war. Building on this foundation, the codebreakers at Bletchley Park achieved what many thought impossible, breaking the complex ciphers that directed German military operations. Ultra intelligence gave the Allies a decisive edge, revealing enemy plans across land and sea. But this success came with a painful dilemma. To protect the Ultra secret and keep the Germans unaware that their codes were compromised, British commanders sometimes allowed friendly ground forces, convoys and ships to be attacked, even when forewarned by decrypted messages. These sacrifices were a heavy burden, but it preserved the vital flow of Ultra intelligence for the rest of the war.","faction":"Britain","type":"order","rarity":"Common","cost":1,"operationCost":0,"attack":0,"defense":0},"defaults":{"UberGraphFrame":{},"Name":"card_event_dilemma","title":{"Namespace":"card_britain","Key":"card_event_dilemma_title","SourceString":"DILEMMA","LocalizedString":"DILEMMA"},"Type":"ETypeEnum::order","faction":"EFactionEnum::Britain","kredits":1,"Text":{"Namespace":"card_britain","Key":"card_event_dilemma_text","SourceString":"Swap the attack and operation cost of target unit.","LocalizedString":"Swap the attack and operation cost of target unit."},"flavorText":{"Namespace":"card_britain","Key":"card_event_dilemma_history","SourceString":